Z||000000||BOSTITCH||08-25-99||11:50 AM||||I too am rebuilding. Curiousity struck me on this one "resized rods" this I have not heard is it nesscesary? Also where did you find those wonderful toys? If I could find those prices I'd be bout done now. <p>Here one I haven't heard discussed, might you smack a vavle with 1.6 roller tips on the 3.1<br>crank?
Z||000001||Stroker||08-25-99||02:58 PM||||BOSTITCH,<br>You'll have to forgive me on the resized rods portion of my parts list.No it is not usually necessary and no, I didn't do it to my 3.2.I have built other engines that needed this done(namely the small block Chevy),so I kinda shoulda thought about it before I posted that part.Sorry.<br> <br>As for the 1.6 ratio roller tips on the 3.1,no I don't believe you will run into a piston with the valve(s) by using that setup.<br>Remember that the stock 2.8 pistons are FLAT TOP and the 3.1 buildup uses DISHED(usually)pistons from a 3.1 motor(like the '90 model CAMARO).Therefore,you have alomost a few extra millimeters of clearance,and unless you have a cam that's got a way high lift there should be no problems.Although don't just ASSUME that it will work.Always,and Imean ALWAYS triple and even quadruple check all engine clearances.The use of clay is a good way to "see" inside the cylinder(s)at full lift.That way you can be sure!<p>As for the prices on the parts I used,I live in AL,where things ain't so spensiv',and I just took the time to find out who had the parts for the BEST price.Most of the bottom end in my engine came from Ken's Auto Parts in Alabaster,AL.They are a first rate independent store that has always impresses me.<p>Well,there you have it,Ihope I've helped some.By the way let us know how your buildup is going!<p>Stroker <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15>
